# What NOT to upload to Vercel. The Python function bundle is built from the
# upload (Python has no tree-shaking), so keep it lean — and NEVER upload a real
# .env: production secrets come from Vercel env vars, not files.

# Secrets — real env files. (frontend/.env.production holds only
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api, which is not a secret, and is intentionally NOT
# matched by these patterns so Vite can read it at build time.)
.env
**/.env
*.env.local

# Python local/dev
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
**/.venv
**/venv
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache

# Backend tests excluded (not needed at runtime). The 48 MB on-disk warm cache
# (backend/app/cache) is INTENTIONALLY shipped: it bundles read-only so warmed
# demo searches (NYC / San Antonio / Glen Rock) serve instantly and, via the
# cached 30-day verdicts, without re-spending the Gemini quota on stage. Writes
# already no-op on Vercel's read-only FS, so shipping it is safe.
backend/tests

# Node / build artifacts (Vercel rebuilds the SPA from source)
**/node_modules
frontend/dist
dist
build

# Old v1 tree, VCS, misc
legacy
.git
*.log
.DS_Store
